---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
import { TRIAL_DAYS } from "@/config/plans";

export const prerender = true;
const l = siteConfig.legal;
---

<LegalLayout title="Terms of service" description={`The terms for using ${siteConfig.name}: accounts, plans and billing, acceptable use, liability and termination.`}>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of {siteConfig.name}, provided by {l.company} ("we"). By creating an account you accept
    them on behalf of yourself or the organization you represent. The service is intended for business customers.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    We provide {siteConfig.name} as described on our website and in the documentation. We may improve the service over time without reducing its core functionality.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Trial and subscription</h2>
  <p>
    New accounts get a {TRIAL_DAYS}-day free trial. After the trial, continued use requires a paid plan. Subscriptions
    renew automatically each month or year until cancelled. If payment fails, we may suspend your account until it
    succeeds. Your data is retained during suspension.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com, which is the merchant of record for all our
    orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns. Prices are shown without VAT, which
    Paddle adds at checkout where applicable. Refunds are covered by our <a href="/refunds">refund policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You must not use the service for unlawful content, malware distribution, attacks on other systems or to infringe
    others' rights. You are responsible for the users you create and the credentials you share.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Your data</h2>
  <p>
    You keep all rights to the content you store. We process it only to provide the service, as your processor under
    Art. 28 GDPR, following your instructions given through the service. We apply appropriate technical and
    organizational measures and notify you without undue delay of any personal data breach.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Availability and support</h2>
  <p>
    We aim for high availability but don't guarantee uninterrupted service. Planned maintenance is announced in advance
    where possible. Support is available at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, our total liability is limited to the fees you paid in the 12 months before the
    claim. We are not liable for indirect or consequential damages. This doesn't limit liability for intent or gross
    negligence.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time from the billing page. The plan stays active until the end of the paid period. After
    termination, your data is deleted within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by Polish law. Courts competent for our registered office have jurisdiction.</p>
</LegalLayout>
